  "preference": "B",
  "rationale": "B is better overall. It puts local publicly funded teacher training (地方公费师范生, admitted in the early batch) at the centre of its advice. That path waives tuition and leads to a guaranteed teaching post back home, which fits the family's limited budget and county-town goal. B also lays out multiple pathways with clear pros and cons, includes pitfalls to avoid, and gives an early-batch plus regular-batch strategy with reach, match and safety tiers. A opens by exposing tool failures, which reads as unprofessional. It mentions publicly funded teacher training only briefly at the end, and it lists 公共事业管理 (public administration) as a medical option. Both contain some score or eligibility inaccuracies, such as B's suggestion of 广州医科大学 and some medical-technology majors for history-track students. Even so, B is more complete, more actionable and better aligned with what the family needs."
